17. MODULE-SPECIFIC ENGINEERING AND SCIENTIFIC REQUIREMENTS
=====================================================================

17.1 NEXUS HYDRO
- Surface water, rivers, lakes, reservoirs and watershed context.
- Groundwater information only at the scale supported by actual datasets.
- Rainfall, water availability, drought and water stress indicators where valid.
- Time-series and historical comparison.
- Water-source and measurement provenance.
- Avoid interpreting GRACE anomalies as local groundwater depth.
- Distinguish observed water levels, modelled estimates and satellite-derived indicators.
- Show missing monitoring coverage.

17.2 NEXUS STRATA
- Geological units, structural features, faults, stratigraphy and available cross-sections.
- Preserve map scale and source.
- Do not fabricate boreholes or subsurface boundaries.
- Distinguish regional geology from site-specific investigation.
- Support natural 3D cutaway only when geometry and data support it.

17.3 NEXUS MINERAL
- Mineral occurrence records and geological context.
- Satellite and geophysical indicators only where source and method support them.
- Never claim a deposit based only on spectral anomalies.
- Distinguish known occurrence, exploration target, indicator and confirmed reserve.
- Include source dates, scale and confidence.

17.4 NEXUS SOIL
- Soil texture, properties, organic carbon, pH and related indicators only when source data supports them.
- Preserve sampling depth and method.
- Distinguish laboratory measurements from gridded estimates.
- Do not claim farm-level precision from coarse global products.
- Explain when field sampling is required.

17.5 NEXUS AGRI
- Crop suitability and agricultural context.
- Climate, soil, water, terrain and land-cover variables.
- Crop calendar and irrigation information where reliable.
- Yield estimates only with documented model and validation.
- Do not guarantee yield, income or crop success.
- Provide practical, evidence-based recommendations with limitations.

17.6 NEXUS ENVIRONMENT
- Land cover and land-use change.
- Environmental indicators and available monitoring records.
- Water/air/soil quality only when real measurements or valid products exist.
- Protected areas and ecosystem context.
- Distinguish observation from attribution.
- Do not claim a nearby facility caused pollution without causal evidence.

17.7 NEXUS CLIMATE
- Historical climate, seasonal patterns and climate indicators.
- Distinguish weather observations, reanalysis, projections and forecasts.
- Show model scenario, time period and spatial scale.
- Do not mix projections with observations without clear labelling.

17.8 NEXUS AI / EIC
- Location-aware, source-grounded question answering.
- Cross-module evidence retrieval.
- Scientific explanations and reports.
- Explicit uncertainty and data-gap analysis.
- No invented facts or unsupported conclusions.

17.9 SHARED DATA CATALOGUE
- Search by location, variable, source, date and resolution.
- Display metadata and licensing.
- Show freshness and source health.
- Allow comparison of compatible datasets.
- Provide data download/export only when terms permit.

